course: dictionary
lesson: 5825
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word maiden is a good example. Its main meaning is a girl or young woman who is not married, often found in old stories. But a ship's maiden voyage is its very first trip, and in cricket a maiden over is one where no runs are scored.
explain: Read the words around the word to choose the meaning. «The famous iron maidens were probably put together in the 1800s, and there is no good evidence they were used in the Middle Ages.» The words put together tell you these are made objects, not girls. So here maiden is part of the name of a thing, and the clues point away from the meaning girl.
explain: Always try the meanings one at a time in the sentence. Does "first" fit? Does "a girl who is not married" fit? The meaning that makes the whole sentence sensible is the right one. If you are still unsure, check a dictionary.
fact: Maiden most often means a girl or young woman who is not married.
fact: «The famous iron maidens were probably put together in the 1800s.» Here maiden is part of a name for an object.
fact: As an adjective, maiden means first, as in a ship's maiden voyage.
fact: A maiden name is the family name a woman had before she married.
fact: In cricket, a maiden over is an over in which no runs are scored.
exercise: «The famous iron maidens were probably put together in the 1800s.» Which clue shows that iron maidens are objects, not girls? | Famous | *Put together | 1800s | Probably
exercise: «The Titanic sank on its maiden voyage.» What does maiden mean here? | Rough | *First | Final | Slow
exercise: In cricket, what is a maiden over? | *An over in which no runs are scored | An over bowled very fast | A over where a wicket falls | An over with extra runs
test: On a form, «mother's maiden name» means the family name she had | after she married | as a baby | in school | *before she married
test: In an old story, a maiden is most likely | a first try | a ship | *a young woman who is not married | a cricket over
exam: In a fairy tale, «a fair maiden in a tower» means | a cricket over with no runs | a ship on its first trip | *a young woman who is not married | a family name
